{"_meta":{"com.oxinsider/docs-group":"games","securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Get game sharp money"},"description":"Where the graded money sits on a whole game, in one read: the S, A and B grade wallets' USD on each side (home, away and, for a 1X2 game, draw) summed across the game's markets, each side's integer share of it, the leader, and wallet counts by grade, plus the backend's verdict on the split. The same aggregate the game page on 0xinsider renders, so the two cannot disagree. Use it instead of paging get_market_holders per market and summing.\n\nArgs:\n  - event_slug (string, required): the game's event slug, for example nba-bos-orl-2026-11-01. Matched case-insensitively\n\nReturns: data with event_slug, status, lifecycle, verdict, allocation, total_usd, unallocated_usd, trader_count, holders_partial, outcomes[] (side, label, usd, pct, is_leader, wallets.s/a/b), computed_at and money_as_of, plus meta. Every aggregate field is null unless status is computed; null means unknown, never zero. verdict.kind is no_sharp_money, all_on, split, leans (label, pct), leans_over_price (label, divergence_pts: how many probability points the money share sits above the price), no_clear_lean, unavailable (money exists but cannot be attributed) or withheld (the money is published but no directional claim is supported). When allocation is degraded, outcomes sum to total_usd minus unallocated_usd and carry no pct or leader. holders_partial true means a market's holder list was a capped page, so counts and dollars cover part of the holders. A settled game returns its recap with lifecycle settled. A game whose aggregate is still computing answers 503 read_model_warming with Retry-After; read again then. A slug with no sports market answers 404. Pro and Max. Descriptive analytics, not an order instruction.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":f